// =====================================================
// 🧩 WHAT THIS SYSTEM IS
// =====================================================
//
// DUME is a deterministic computation kernel for structured vector systems
// with enforced integrity semantics.
//
// It provides:
// - replayable execution
// - verifiable state transitions
// - cryptographic auditability
// - storage-agnostic persistence
// - manifold-aware structural hooks
//
// It is not a database or vector search tool in the traditional sense.
// It is a deterministic state evolution engine.
//
// =====================================================
// ✔ CORE SYSTEM CAPABILITIES
// =====================================================

/*
🧮 1. DETERMINISTIC EXECUTION ENGINE (STRICT CORE)

- Monotonic ingestion ordering
- Fully replayable system state
- Explicit envelope-based state transitions
- No hidden mutation paths
- No probabilistic branching

This defines the computational truth layer of DUME.
*/

/*
🛡 2. DUMEGOV — GOVERNANCE & VERIFICATION LAYER

- Policy enforcement pre/post execution
- Drift and entropy validation
- Tamper-evident audit logging
- Actor-bound cryptographic signatures
- Integrity verification independent of compute path

DUMEgov does NOT compute state.
It verifies state correctness.
*/

/*
💾 3. STORAGE ABSTRACTION LAYER

- Backend-agnostic persistence interface
- Supports memory, disk, distributed storage
- Enables deterministic replay across environments
- Preserves immutable envelope semantics

Storage is replaceable without engine modification.
*/

/*
🧬 4. COMPRESSION + MANIFOLD HOOKS

- Sparse vector compression at ingestion
- Entropy- and drift-aware transformations
- Pluggable manifold learning interfaces
- Future-ready structural projection system

Defines how raw data becomes structured state.
*/

/*
🌐 5. GOSSIP TRANSPORT LAYER

- Ordered delta emission system
- Event propagation for distributed clusters
- Eventual consistency scaffolding
- Non-authoritative design (no truth ownership)

This is a transport abstraction, not a consensus layer.
*/

/*
🔁 6. REPLAYABLE STATE SYSTEM

- Full system reconstruction from logs
- Deterministic re-execution across nodes
- No reliance on runtime memory state
- Audit-driven state validation

Replay is a core feature, not a debugging tool.
*/

/*
🔐 7. CRYPTOGRAPHIC AUDIT CHAIN

- SHA-based envelope hashing
- Linked hash-chain history
- Merkle-style checkpoint support
- Actor-bound zoned signatures
- Tamper-evident system evolution tracking

This is the system trust backbone.
*/

